Z||000000||MickeyAsh||11-30-2001||10:47 PM||||So, I cant leave well enough alone, eh? First hard starting, and now I have a nasty knock in the good ol' 2.8v6... Here's the scoop... I adjusted Top Dead Center for Cyl#1 today, along with perfecting the timing, also replaced my Idle Air Control because it was throwing me some codes. Cranked her up, no problems, better acceleration than ever before with no bad news to report... as I'm pulling into my apt complex, I hear a knocking consitent with my RPM, and I went pale I'm sure. Before I play around with the TDC again to double check... is knocking always a one way street to rebuild/transplant city, or could it be that my spark plug is firing while the piston(s) are still on their ascent up to TDC, causing that horrifying knock of my wallet opening? Please god tell me it's just the TDC arrangement... thanks in advance for the help, again... ||||reg||9
Z||000001||GT GT 87||11-30-2001||11:47 PM||||If you changed timing and now have a knock----------you couldn't have a bad bearing that fast !!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||anatodigit||12-01-2001||12:48 AM||||alright   this might sound weird   but was your heat on?<BR>I had a loud knocking sound coming from my 2.8. thought i was looking at a rebuild    but then I turned the heater off and put it to cold   and the knocking stopped.  Every time i put the heat on   it starts knocking again  ||||reg||5
Z||000003||MickeyAsh||12-01-2001||09:17 AM||||Nah my heat isnt on, it's 70* here at night, coldest 65* at like 8am.... plus my heater core is looped off cuz i didnt have cash to replace it when the last one started peeing on my interior... but it could be my timing then in theory?||||reg||1
Z||000004||maryjane||12-01-2001||12:16 PM||||I'd sure try changing the timing back a little or rechecking it EXACTLY by the proper procedure before going for a rebuild/replacement. How much did you have to change the timing to achieve the correct timing average? You know you are supposed to ground the 2 terminal (A & B I think) on the alcl and take the average between  #1 & # 4<BR>cyls. Exact instructions are on a tag under the rear deck lid and in the manuals.<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 12-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||MickeyAsh||12-01-2001||08:56 PM||||Well I spent all day adjusting and readjusting the timing and TDC in every imaginable manner including Haynes instructions, stuff on the net, and my own random ideas, yet the noise is still there and it's very very nasty sounding... already starting to look at my rebuild options... it fires perfectly, doesnt miss a beat, great pickup and accel, but the knocking is still present, honestly it's driving great, but the knocking is enough to scare me into not driving it for fear of damage...||||reg||1
